  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Four of a Kind (Vying / Betting). Setup: 4-8 players, ante. Deal: 1 unique face-up card per player. Win condition: First to 4 matching cards wins 50% of pot. Other 50%: lowest total hand value (by card ranks). Play: Cards revealed one at a time. Matches go to owner. Betting rounds after initial deal and each match. Fold is legal. Card values: A=14, K=13, Q=12, J=11, 10-2=face value.',
    Player: "Welcome to Four of a Kind. Each player starts with one unique card face-up. You're trying to collect all four cards of your rank. As cards are revealed, if yours match you take them. Betting happens at the start and after each match. Winner takes 50% of the pot. Lowest total hand takes the other 50%.",
    objective: 'Collect all four cards of your starting rank OR hold the lowest total hand when someone else completes their set.',
    gameplay: "1. First Betting: After the initial cards are dealt, the player with the highest card starts the betting.\n2. The Reveal: The dealer turns cards from the undealt deck one at a time.\n3. Matching: If the turned card matches a player's rank, that player takes the card.\n4. Betting Rounds: Every time a match occurs, a new round of betting begins, led by the player with the most cards (or highest rank if tied).\n5. Discards: If a card doesn't match anyone's held rank, it is discarded, and the next card is flipped.",
    keyRules: [
      'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Four of a Kind.',
      'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Two-pot system: High pot (four-of-a-kind or best hand) and Low pot (lowest 5-card hand).',
      'Winning condition: Collect all four cards of your starting rank OR hold the lowest total hand when someone else completes their set.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '4 to 8 players. Optimal at 6-8.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. Aces rank high.',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card deck. Aces rank high.',
      dealing: 'deal and betting Each player places the agreed ante into the pot.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. First Betting: After the initial cards are dealt, the player with the highest card starts the betting.\n2. The Reveal: The dealer turns cards from the undealt deck one at a time.\n3. Matching: If the turned card matches a player's rank, that player takes the card.\n4. Betting Rounds: Every time a match occurs, a new round of betting begins, led by the player with the most cards (or highest rank if tied).\n5. Discards: If a card doesn't match anyone's held rank, it is discarded, and the next card is flipped.",
